WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.390
Two acids, at exactly the same concentration:
25.0 cubic centimetres of each.

2
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.170
Titrate each with the same alkali,

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.490
and both need exactly the same
volume to reach equivalence.

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:17.310
Yet one of them is a strong
acid, and the other is weak.

5
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.670
So how can a titration
show which one is weak?

6
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.050
In this mission, you'll meet
the four shapes of pH curve,

7
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.250
for every pairing of strong
and weak acids and bases.

8
00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.750
You'll find the intercept,

9
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.750
the equivalence point and the
half-equivalence point, and read off a p K a.

10
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.390
Your mission: explain how a
titration curve reveals a weak acid.
